# prologue: who is met on the way in, for a new life to answer before the first town (the owner, 6 November: a brief playable opening, not a told one; 7 November: someone met on the road, with a decision that reveals your character early).
// A Kyr template (see src/world/kyr-template.ts), written into an origin's module (see src/world/origins.ts) at the way
// into the first town ({approach}); one option drawn for each country by its seed. Each is someone met with something
// that wants deciding, and more than one answer to it: help, strike a bargain, take what is going, stand up to
// someone, or walk on. One a calling can meet that another cannot (a thief's quiet hands, a liar's tongue). What was
// answered stays with the company: something in hand, a fact of what it did that it knows of itself (its notes keep
// it, as the town will), and whoever was met going on to {home}'s inn ({inn}, the inn's taproom), where they remember.
// The opening sets the meeting apart before the first place (see Prologue): the `meeting`, said near whoever is met,
// and every act of theirs whose id begins with theirs (carter_…, poacher_…) as its answers, until `answered(party)`.
// {home} is the town; {folk} its people. Add an option to add a meeting; nothing in the engine needs to change.
--- base
  // The town's inn, where whoever was met goes on to, is the origin's own (the region's taproom: see Origins.write).
  // What was done on the way in, once; and whether whoever was met there has been answered, one way or another.
  Relation wayIn(entity). Relation answered(group).
--- road carter 2
  // A carter whose wheel has gone off the crown of the road into the ditch: lead the horse while he heaves, ask a
  // share of the load for it, walk on; or, while his back is to you, take something off it. What was done goes into
  // {home} with him.
  Person carter "the wagoner" at {approach} {
    Role "a wagoner hauling meal into {home}". Ancestry {folk}. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner grim.
    // Spoken to once the wheel is out, not as a stranger's: "If it's trouble, I have enough of my own" had greeted
    // whoever had just got him out of the ditch (three cold rounds running: R3-C, R4-E 18, R4-F 19).
    Greets "The wagoner wipes his hands on his coat. 'Thank you,' he says." when state(cart, righted).
    // While the wheel is still in the ditch, spoken to, he says what he wants: talking to him then had shown an empty
    // page in every walk that tried it (PP-07).
    Greets "The wagoner looks up from the wheel. 'If you're stopping, take the horse's head,' he says. 'If not, go on.'" when state(cart, ditched).
  }
  Observe meeting near carter when not answered(party) "A cart has slid off the road. One wheel is in the ditch up to the hub, and the horse is straining in the shafts. The wagoner stands in the ditch, pushing at the wheel with his shoulder. He looks up as you come, but he does not ask for help.".
  Thing cart "the cart" at {approach} {
    // Only what the meeting does not say: the cart was told twice, word for word nearly, on the road in (the headless
    // terminal, 12 November).
    State ditched "Sacks of meal are roped on the cart. One has split, and meal is spilling into the ditch.".
    State righted "The cart is back on the road, and the horse stands quiet.".
    Change heave "Heave the wheel out with him" from ditched to righted needing brawn or crowbar.
    }
  Topic carter_thanks with carter "Hear the wagoner's thanks" when state(cart, righted) and not wayIn(cart_righted) and not wayIn(cart_bargained) once {
    Says "'Eat at the inn tonight, at my cost,' says the wagoner. 'Ask for me there. I'll be in before you.' He gives you two coins as well, and will not take them back.".
    On discuss { Assert wayIn(cart_righted). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 2. }
  }
  // However it came out of the ditch, it was answered.
  Rule carter_answered when state(cart, righted) and not answered(party) { Assert answered(party). }
  // The cart on the road again, the carter goes on into {home} ahead of whoever is still on the way in, to the inn.
  Rule carter_goes_on when state(cart, righted) and at(carter, {approach}) and not at(party, {approach}) {
    Retract at(carter, {approach}). Assert at(carter, {inn}).
  }
  // Said as what he gave (he pressed two coins on you, and would not have them back): it had said you took nothing
  // but his thanks, under the two coins (Mission 20's third round, C 24).
  Entity cart_righted: fact "On the way into {home} you got a wagoner's wheel out of the ditch.".
  // What the company did, known as done: learnt from his thanks, it had been filed as the wagoner's word, "told you,
  // not yet seen for yourself" (two cold rounds and the owner's play of 10 November).
  // Once: it had been said wherever the wagoner was, five times by the evening and again after a reload (round 7).
  Observe carter_deed near carter when state(cart, righted) and not wayIn(cart_bargained) and not knows(party, cart_righted) "You helped the wagoner get his cart out of the ditch." teaches cart_righted.
  Entity cart_bargained: fact "On the way into {home} you got a wagoner out of the ditch for a sack of his meal and a coin.".
  Entity cart_left: fact "On the way into {home} you left a wagoner in the ditch, and did not stop.".
  Entity cart_robbed: fact "On the way into {home} you lifted a sack off a wagoner's load while his back was to you.".
  // Anyone can take the horse's head while he heaves: slower, and the horse has its own mind. Not once the meeting is
  // answered otherwise: a sack lifted off his load, the horse's head had still been offered, and his thanks after it
  // (round 6, the register's WM-03).
  Action carter_lead(actor: group, site: place) "Lead the horse while he heaves" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {approach}) and state(cart, ditched)
      and not answered(actor).
    Time 3.
    On success { Retract state(cart, ditched). Assert state(cart, righted). Assert answered(actor). }
    Result "You take the horse by the bridle and lead it forward while the wagoner pushes on the wheel. The cart comes up out of the ditch and back onto the road.".
  }
  // One who can go unseen can lift a sack while his back is to the road: something to sell, and a man in {home} who
  // counts his sacks.
  Action carter_lift(actor: group, site: place) "Steal a sack of meal off the cart" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {approach}) and capable(actor, stealth) and state(cart, ditched) and not wayIn(cart_robbed).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert wayIn(cart_robbed). Assert answered(actor). Assert knows(actor, cart_robbed). Give rations to actor. }
    Result "You lift a sack off the back of the cart. The wagoner is pushing at the wheel and does not turn round.".
  }
  // A hand for a price: a sack of the meal and a coin, and the wagoner's opinion of you.
  // A bargain struck, not thanks owed: said to him, and done (an act, so that the wagoner is not badged as owing
  // before anything is done for him: Owed reads what a topic would pay).
  Action carter_bargain(actor: group, site: place) "Help him, for a share of the load" {
    Speaker carter.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(carter, site) and state(cart, ditched) and not answered(actor).
    Time 3.
    On success { Retract state(cart, ditched). Assert state(cart, righted). Assert wayIn(cart_bargained). Assert answered(actor).
      Assert knows(actor, cart_bargained). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 1. Give rations to actor. }
    Result "'A share?' says the wagoner. 'A sack of meal and a coin, then. Be quick.' You push the wheel with him while the horse pulls, and the cart comes up out of the ditch. He gives you the sack and the coin, and says nothing more.".
  }
  Topic carter_leave with carter "Leave him to it" when state(cart, ditched) and not wayIn(cart_left) once {
    Says "The wagoner says nothing. He turns back to his wheel.".
    On discuss { Assert wayIn(cart_left). Assert answered(actor). Assert knows(actor, cart_left). }
  }
  // A question, not an answer: kept out of the meeting's answers by its id (Prologue.meeting takes carter_…).
  Topic ask_wagoner with carter "Ask the wagoner what he is carrying, and where" when state(cart, ditched) once {
    Says "'Meal for {home},' he says. 'I'm late with it already. Three days on the road, and the wheel goes in the ditch a mile from town. Can you give me a hand?'".
  }
  // In {home}, at the inn, what was done on the road is remembered.
  // Helped out of the ditch, he would come along: what was done on the road is who will walk beside the company (the owner, 19 November: the very first choices, to help someone or not and to go with companions or alone, the one
  // met on the road someone who could come along; AT-08).
  Topic carter_come with carter "Ask the wagoner whether he would come with you" when at(carter, {inn}) and (wayIn(cart_righted) or wayIn(cart_bargained)) and not willing(carter, actor) and not travelsWith(carter, actor) once {
    Says "The wagoner turns his cup on the board. 'The meal's sold. The cart can stand till market day. I've a strong back, and I know the roads. I'll come.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(carter, actor). Set hire(carter) to 0. }
  }
  Topic carter_inn with carter "Sit with the wagoner" when at(carter, {inn}) and wayIn(cart_righted) once {
    Says "'Here's the one,' says the wagoner to the room, and pushes a bowl along the board to you. 'Got me out of the ditch at the top of the hill. Eat.' He knows the road and the town both. He talks while you eat.".
    On discuss { Retract hungry(actor). }
  }
--- road poacher 2
  // A poacher's boy with a hare in a snare and the keeper up the road: talk the keeper past him, hold him for the
  // keeper, buy the hare, or walk on. A liar's tongue is tried; anyone can be honest, or buy, or go by.
  Person poacher "the boy" at {approach} {
    Role "a boy down in the bracken with a hare in a snare". Ancestry {folk}. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
  }
  Observe meeting near poacher when not answered(party) "A boy is kneeling in the bracken by the road. He has a hare in a wire snare. Up the road a man whistles twice and calls a dog. It is the gamekeeper, and the hare is his master's. If the keeper finds the boy with it, the boy will be taken for a poacher. The boy holds the hare against his chest and looks at you.".
  Entity hare_hidden: fact "On the way into {home} you stood in the road and talked the keeper past a poacher's boy.".
  Entity hare_given: fact "On the way into {home} you held a poacher's boy for the keeper, who paid you for it.".
  Entity hare_bought: fact "On the way into {home} you bought a snared hare off a poacher's boy, the keeper's whistle coming.".
  Entity hare_left: fact "On the way into {home} you walked past a poacher's boy and left him to the keeper.".
  Action poacher_cover(actor: group, site: place) "Keep the keeper talking" {
    Speaker poacher.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(poacher, site) and not answered(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert answered(actor). Assert wayIn(hare_hidden). Assert knows(actor, hare_hidden). Give rations to actor. }
    On failure { Assert answered(actor). Assert wayIn(hare_hidden). Assert knows(actor, hare_hidden). }
    Result "'Keeper,' you say, and he stops to hear what you want. By the time you have asked him the way to {home} twice over, the bracken is empty. Further on, on a stone where you cannot miss it, someone has left the hare. It is a day's eating, and goes into the pack with the rest of the food.".
    Otherwise "The keeper hears you out. He looks past you at the bracken, and back at you. The boy is gone. The keeper will know your face again.".
  }
  Topic poacher_hold with poacher "Hold the boy for the keeper" when not answered(actor) once {
    Says "The boy struggles, and then goes still. The keeper comes up through the bracken with his dog. He takes the hare and the boy's ear in one hand, and gives you two coin with the other. 'There's few on this road would,' he says. The boy looks back at you once, going.".
    On discuss { Assert answered(actor). Assert wayIn(hare_given). Assert knows(actor, hare_given). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 2. }
  }
  Topic poacher_buy with poacher "Buy the hare for a coin" when not answered(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 1 once {
    // The hare is a day's eating, given as rations: said so, where it had been put in the player's hands and was then
    // nowhere in the pack (round 12, B: T24-19).
    Says "He looks at the coin, and at the road. He puts the hare in your hands and the coin in his mouth. He is gone into the bracken before the whistle comes again. It is a fat hare, and a day's eating: it goes into the pack with the rest of the food.".
    On discuss { Assert answered(actor). Assert wayIn(hare_bought). Assert knows(actor, hare_bought). Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 1. Give rations to actor. }
  }
  Topic poacher_leave with poacher "Leave the boy to it" when not answered(actor) once {
    Says "Some way behind you, a dog gives tongue. Somebody yells.".
    On discuss { Assert answered(actor). Assert wayIn(hare_left). Assert knows(actor, hare_left). }
  }
  // Whatever came of it, the boy turns up in {home}, unless the keeper has him; one who stood in the road for him is
  // owed, and paid. He is off the road at once, as what is said of him says: he had been told as here, under the
  // words that had him gone into the bracken (round 12, B: T24-19); and one the keeper took is gone with the keeper.
  Rule poacher_goes_on when answered(party) and at(poacher, {approach}) and not wayIn(hare_given) {
    Retract at(poacher, {approach}). Assert at(poacher, {inn}).
  }
  Rule poacher_taken when wayIn(hare_given) and at(poacher, {approach}) { Retract at(poacher, {approach}). }
  // Hidden from the keeper, he would come along (the owner, 19 November: the very first choices, to help someone or not and to go with companions or alone, the one
  // met on the road someone who could come along; AT-08).
  Topic poacher_come with poacher "Ask the boy whether he would come with you" when at(poacher, {inn}) and wayIn(hare_hidden) and not willing(poacher, actor) and not travelsWith(poacher, actor) once {
    Says "The boy looks at you a long moment. 'Nobody here wants me. I can go quiet. I hit what I throw at. I'll come.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(poacher, actor). Set hire(poacher) to 0. }
  }
  Topic poacher_inn with poacher "Sit with the boy" when at(poacher, {inn}) and wayIn(hare_hidden) once {
    Says "He sits down beside you on the bench. 'That was my brother's,' he says. He puts a sling on the board in front of you, the stones in a twist of cloth. 'He's no use for it now. You keep it.' Then he is gone again, with half your bread.".
    On discuss { Give sling to actor. }
  }
--- road pedlar 2
  // A pedlar being robbed on the road: stand up to the two men, buy them off, help yourself with them, or keep to the
  // far side and walk on. What a pedlar's pack holds goes to whoever ends up with it; the pedlar tells the inn.
  Person pedlar "the pedlar" at {approach} {
    Role "a pedlar sitting in the ditch with a hand to his head". Ancestry {folk}. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
  }
  // The two men are people of the road, there to be fought if it comes to it (OR-146, the owner's playtest of 20
  // November: a defeat had been narrated, "one shove", with no fight and no hurt). Not killers: a fight with them is a
  // bout (yields), over at the first fall, and whoever loses it is the worse for wear.
  Person robbers "the two robbers" at {approach} {
    Role "two men of the road with the pedlar's pack open between them". Ancestry {folk}. Calling commoner. Numbers 2. Level 1. Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    Called "the bigger robber", "the smaller robber".
    Comes "The bigger of them comes at you with his fists up, and the other picks up the pedlar's stick.".
  }
  Initially Assert yields(robbers).
  Observe meeting near pedlar when not answered(party) "Two men are robbing a pedlar: they have his pack open in the middle of the road, and are going through it. The pedlar sits in the ditch with a hand to his head, blood between the fingers. One of them holds a lantern up to the light and laughs. Then they see you, and stop laughing. They wait to see what you are.".
  Entity pack_saved: fact "On the way into {home} you stood up to two men robbing a pedlar on the road.".
  Entity pack_bought: fact "On the way into {home} you paid off two men robbing a pedlar.".
  Entity pack_shared: fact "On the way into {home} you took a pedlar's lantern while two men robbed him.".
  Entity pack_left: fact "On the way into {home} you kept to the far side of the road while a pedlar was robbed.".
  Action pedlar_stand(actor: group, site: place) "Stand up to the robbers" {
    Speaker pedlar.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pedlar, site) and not answered(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, intimidation, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert answered(actor). Assert wayIn(pack_saved). Assert knows(actor, pack_saved). Give lantern to actor. Retract at(robbers, {approach}). }
    On failure { Assert answered(actor). Assert wayIn(pack_saved). Assert knows(actor, pack_saved). Retract peaceable(robbers). Assert assails(robbers, actor). }
    Result "They look at you, and at each other. They drop the lantern in the road and go off over the field without hurrying. The pedlar gets up, picks the lantern out of the mud, and puts it in your hands. 'Keep it. It's the least of what they'd have had.'".
    Otherwise "They look at each other and laugh. 'Two of us,' says the bigger, and puts the lantern down.".
  }
  // The bout, won: they break and run, and the lantern is the pedlar's to give. Lost: the company is the worse for it
  // (the hurt is the fight's own), and they go with a fistful of the pack.
  Rule robbers_run when routed(robbers) and at(robbers, {approach}) says "The two of them break and run over the field, the smaller one holding his ribs. The pedlar gets up, picks the lantern out of the mud, and puts it in your hands. 'Keep it,' he says. 'You earned it the hard way.'" {
    Retract at(robbers, {approach}). Give lantern to party.
  }
  Rule robbers_win when yielded(party, robbers) and at(robbers, {approach}) says "You are sitting in the road with blood in your mouth. They go off over the field laughing, with a fistful of the pack. The pedlar helps you up. 'Brave,' he says, 'and a fool. I'll say so at the inn, both.'" {
    Retract at(robbers, {approach}).
  }
  // Paid, helped or walked past, they go on their way with what they have.
  Rule robbers_go when answered(party) and peaceable(robbers) and at(robbers, {approach}) { Retract at(robbers, {approach}). }
  Topic pedlar_pay with pedlar "Pay the robbers three coin" when not answered(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 3 once {
    Says "The one with the lantern weighs your coin in one hand and the lantern in the other. He tosses the lantern into the ditch beside the pedlar. 'Fair,' he says, and they go. The pedlar is a long time thanking you. He gives you a flask of lamp oil out of the pack for what you paid.".
    On discuss { Assert answered(actor). Assert wayIn(pack_bought). Assert knows(actor, pack_bought). Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Give lamp_oil to actor. }
  }
  Topic pedlar_share with pedlar "Help yourself to the pack" when not answered(actor) once {
    Says "'Now there's a sensible face,' says the one with the lantern, and lets you have it. You go on into {home} with it. Behind you the pedlar watches you go, and says nothing.".
    On discuss { Assert answered(actor). Assert wayIn(pack_shared). Assert knows(actor, pack_shared). Give lantern to actor. }
  }
  Topic pedlar_leave with pedlar "Leave the pedlar to them" when not answered(actor) once {
    Says "Nobody stops you, and you walk on past.".
    On discuss { Assert answered(actor). Assert wayIn(pack_left). Assert knows(actor, pack_left). }
  }
  Rule pedlar_goes_on when answered(party) and at(pedlar, {approach}) and not at(party, {approach}) {
    Retract at(pedlar, {approach}). Assert at(pedlar, {inn}).
  }
  // His pack saved on the road, or bought back, he would come along; never with one who helped themselves to it (the owner, 19 November: the very first choices, to help someone or not and to go with companions or alone, the one
  // met on the road someone who could come along; AT-08).
  Topic pedlar_come with pedlar "Ask the pedlar whether he would come with you" when at(pedlar, {inn}) and (wayIn(pack_saved) or wayIn(pack_bought)) and not willing(pedlar, actor) and not travelsWith(pedlar, actor) once {
    Says "The pedlar touches the bandage on his head. 'The pack can wait with the innkeeper. I know every road hereabouts. I'd sooner walk with someone who stops for a man in a ditch.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(pedlar, actor). Set hire(pedlar) to 0. }
  }
  Topic pedlar_inn with pedlar "Sit with the pedlar" when at(pedlar, {inn}) and (wayIn(pack_saved) or wayIn(pack_bought)) once {
    Says "The pedlar has a clean bandage round his head and a jug in front of him, and pushes it across. 'They'll not be back on this road while you're on it,' he says. 'That's worth a drink.' He knows every door in {home} that buys, and which of them pays.".
    On discuss { Retract hungry(actor). }
  }
  Observe pedlar_tells near pedlar when at(pedlar, {inn}) and wayIn(pack_shared) "The pedlar from the road is at a table by the door. He sees you come in, and says something to the people with him. They all turn and look at you.".
